1
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:05,179
[siren wailing]

2
00:00:12,795 --> 00:00:13,970
Oh.

3
00:00:18,496 --> 00:00:20,194
[Jane]
What's the fuss?

4
00:00:20,281 --> 00:00:22,457
[Cho]
Slept through Lisbon's
briefing in the van, didn't you?

5
00:00:23,849 --> 00:00:25,416
Like a baby.

6
00:00:25,503 --> 00:00:27,114
[Cho]
Yeah, the victim's
name is Kristin Marley.

7
00:00:27,201 --> 00:00:28,593
She worked at the State Capitol
for some lady senator.

8
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:30,204
Went missing three days ago.

9
00:00:30,291 --> 00:00:31,422
Rumor is she was
having an affair

10
00:00:31,509 --> 00:00:33,903
'with the senator's husband.'

11
00:00:40,214 --> 00:00:42,564
- My bet. She's a jumper.
- I hope not.

12
00:00:42,651 --> 00:00:44,087
If she's a jumper,
job's done.

13
00:00:44,174 --> 00:00:45,567
Yeah, the senator's husband
dumps her

14
00:00:45,654 --> 00:00:47,395
she wants to make him feel bad,
she comes out here..

15
00:00:47,482 --> 00:00:48,831
[whistles]
...splat.

16
00:00:48,918 --> 00:00:50,702
Don't talk that way.

17
00:00:50,789 --> 00:00:53,575
Okay, not splat. Bam.

18
00:00:53,662 --> 00:00:56,404
There's nothing worse than
suicide. Human life is sacred.

19
00:00:56,491 --> 00:00:59,015
When someone takes
their own life, it's a tragedy.

20
00:00:59,102 --> 00:01:01,496
Sacramento PD's
handing the case over to us.

21
00:01:01,583 --> 00:01:05,152
Let's go talk
to the coroner.

22
00:01:05,239 --> 00:01:08,677
Shall I recap
the case, sleepyhead?

23
00:01:08,764 --> 00:01:12,072
Kristin Marley,
lady senator's aide

24
00:01:12,159 --> 00:01:14,726
rumored romance
with the senator's husband.

25
00:01:14,813 --> 00:01:15,988
Very good.

26
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:18,034
Oh, I trained myself
to hear

27
00:01:18,121 --> 00:01:21,255
and take in information
while asleep.

28
00:01:21,342 --> 00:01:23,474
- The others told you?
- Yes, they did.

29
00:01:23,561 --> 00:01:25,520
[male #1]
At this point,
there's no way to determine

30
00:01:25,607 --> 00:01:27,261
what happened
to the victim, Agent Lisbon.

31
00:01:27,348 --> 00:01:29,045
I-I simply can't help you.

32
00:01:29,132 --> 00:01:30,699
Well, can you tell
how long she's been dead?

33
00:01:30,786 --> 00:01:33,441
[scoffs]
Couldn't possibly
given the evidence available.

34
00:01:33,528 --> 00:01:35,356
Well, do you think it was
a homicide or a suicide?

35
00:01:35,443 --> 00:01:38,054
- 'Couldn't say.'
- 'What's your guess?'

36
00:01:38,141 --> 00:01:41,710
I'm not in the habit
of, of guessing.

37
00:01:41,797 --> 00:01:43,364
Please don't touch
the decedent.

38
00:01:43,451 --> 00:01:46,106
Y-you detectives always
want the instant answers.

39
00:01:46,193 --> 00:01:47,498
What I do is science.

40
00:01:47,585 --> 00:01:49,326
Science will...uncover the truth

41
00:01:49,413 --> 00:01:53,722
but she will be precise,
methodical and take her time

42
00:01:53,809 --> 00:01:55,680
before she renders
her decision.

43
00:01:55,767 --> 00:01:58,292
Wonder if science can remove
the stick from his butt.

44
00:01:58,379 --> 00:02:00,946
- I heard that.
- You're right. We want facts.

45
00:02:01,033 --> 00:02:02,209
Fortunately, we have them.

46
00:02:02,296 --> 00:02:03,906
Oh, we do?

47
00:02:03,993 --> 00:02:06,300
In abundance.

48
00:02:06,387 --> 00:02:07,518
You're the consultant
that pretends

49
00:02:07,605 --> 00:02:09,477
to read minds, aren't you?

50
00:02:09,564 --> 00:02:11,392
No. I don't pretend
to read minds.

51
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:12,784
Idoread minds.

52
00:02:12,871 --> 00:02:13,916
But don't we all?
Look at Lisbon.

53
00:02:14,003 --> 00:02:15,352
You can see
what she's thinking.

54
00:02:15,439 --> 00:02:16,832
No kidding.

55
00:02:19,313 --> 00:02:21,097
And I can see what
you're thinking right now.

56
00:02:21,184 --> 00:02:24,840
Uh, I-I was thinking that
you, sir, are a bumptious fool

57
00:02:24,927 --> 00:02:26,929
and I was wondering
exactly what training

58
00:02:27,016 --> 00:02:28,800
in forensic pathology you have.

59
00:02:28,887 --> 00:02:30,933
Ah, but right before that,
you were wondering

60
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:34,284
whether you would choose Lisbon
or Van Pelt as your concubine

61
00:02:34,371 --> 00:02:38,245
in that little fantasy kingdom
you like to visit sometimes.

62
00:02:38,332 --> 00:02:40,072
What? I do not.

63
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,813
Oh, and-nd you're right.

64
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:44,338
I-I know nothing
of forensic pathology.

65
00:02:44,425 --> 00:02:46,557
'But agent Van Pelt..'

66
00:02:46,644 --> 00:02:49,821
...she might offer...her theory.

67
00:02:49,908 --> 00:02:51,214
Or I might not.

68
00:02:51,301 --> 00:02:53,564
- Look at her feet.
- I did.

69
00:02:53,651 --> 00:02:55,566
And what question
presents itself?

70
00:02:59,091 --> 00:03:00,789
- Where's her other shoe?
- Exactly.

71
00:03:00,876 --> 00:03:01,877
[Cho]
'It wasn't
up on the bridge.'

72
00:03:01,964 --> 00:03:03,444
It could be in her car.

73
00:03:03,531 --> 00:03:04,967
Even if it was,
why would she walk to

74
00:03:05,054 --> 00:03:06,360
the middle of the bridge
with one shoe on?

75
00:03:06,447 --> 00:03:08,362
- Why would she do that?
- Bingo.

76
00:03:08,449 --> 00:03:10,320
There's no need
to be patronizing.

77
00:03:10,407 --> 00:03:12,453
So she must have been carried.

78
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:14,933
She didn't kill herself. She was
murdered, then dropped over.

79
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:16,892
Or thrown over still alive.

80
00:03:16,979 --> 00:03:18,763
Better than suicide.

81
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:22,724
It's...a theory.

82
00:03:22,811 --> 00:03:24,160
It's lovely to meet you, doc.

83
00:03:24,247 --> 00:03:25,988
You're a horse's ass,
but you mean well.

84
00:03:26,075 --> 00:03:29,165
- I'll be in the van.
- Oh.

85
00:03:29,252 --> 00:03:31,167
My apologies, sir.

86
00:03:31,254 --> 00:03:34,475
Cho, tell the Sacramento PD
that it's a homicide.

87
00:03:34,562 --> 00:03:36,694
Rigsby, Van Pelt, see what
the sheriff's department

88
00:03:36,781 --> 00:03:38,914
got in their investigation.

89
00:03:39,001 --> 00:03:40,307
[Rigsby]
Alright.

90
00:03:42,004 --> 00:03:44,398
[theme music]

91
00:03:58,542 --> 00:04:01,415
Kristin had been interning
here for about nine months.

92
00:04:01,502 --> 00:04:03,112
She came in at the start
of the last session

93
00:04:03,199 --> 00:04:04,766
right out of college.

94
00:04:04,853 --> 00:04:08,030
I liked her. She was sweet,
young, in a good way.

95
00:04:08,117 --> 00:04:10,641
- Who did she work for?
- Senator Melinda Batson.

96
00:04:10,728 --> 00:04:14,384
'She's an up-and-comer
from the Central Valley.'

97
00:04:14,471 --> 00:04:16,343
Please put that down.

98
00:04:18,823 --> 00:04:20,390
Anything to the rumor
that Kristin was having

99
00:04:20,477 --> 00:04:22,044
an affair
with Batson's husband?

100
00:04:22,131 --> 00:04:25,569
Elliott Batson.
He's Melinda's chief of staff.

101
00:04:25,656 --> 00:04:27,919
We've heard the rumors.
Everyone denies it.

102
00:04:28,006 --> 00:04:29,834
There's no evidence
anything happened.

103
00:04:29,921 --> 00:04:32,010
The media
seem to think there is.

104
00:04:32,097 --> 00:04:34,796
You wanna get me started
on what they believe?

105
00:04:34,883 --> 00:04:36,841
Frankly, when you've worked
here as long as I have

106
00:04:36,928 --> 00:04:39,714
you hear a lot of stories
about wild behavior.

107
00:04:39,801 --> 00:04:41,063
Most of them aren't true.

108
00:04:41,150 --> 00:04:42,325
[amplified]
Except the ones that are.

109
00:04:42,412 --> 00:04:43,500
[microphone feedback whines]
Whoa.

110
00:04:43,587 --> 00:04:44,719
'Sorry.'

111
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:50,507
Hello.

112
00:04:50,594 --> 00:04:52,292
Hello. Hello. Hello.

113
00:04:55,077 --> 00:04:57,209
I've issued a statement, and
I'm not taking any questions.

114
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:59,908
We're not press.
We're CBI.

115
00:04:59,995 --> 00:05:02,345
Agent Teresa Lisbon,
Patrick Jane.

116
00:05:02,432 --> 00:05:05,261
Right. Sorry. You called.

117
00:05:05,348 --> 00:05:07,698
Melinda Batson.

118
00:05:07,785 --> 00:05:09,657
This is my husband Elliott.

119
00:05:09,744 --> 00:05:11,615
Hi.

120
00:05:11,702 --> 00:05:13,878
Tsk. Tough day around here.

121
00:05:18,361 --> 00:05:19,667
Is this Kristin's desk?

122
00:05:19,754 --> 00:05:21,669
- Yes.
- Mm.

123
00:05:21,756 --> 00:05:24,411
Come inside.

124
00:05:28,066 --> 00:05:29,720
Jane.

125
00:05:29,807 --> 00:05:32,070
- Care to join us?
- I'll be right there.

126
00:05:48,304 --> 00:05:50,088
Anything unusual
about Kristin's behavior

127
00:05:50,175 --> 00:05:52,090
the day she disappeared?

128
00:05:52,177 --> 00:05:54,528
No, she was, uh, cheerful.

129
00:05:54,615 --> 00:05:57,357
Finished work, left at 6:00,
I think, uh..

130
00:05:57,444 --> 00:05:59,837
- A little after 6:00.
- After 6:00 then.

131
00:05:59,924 --> 00:06:01,883
Did she say
where she was going?

132
00:06:01,970 --> 00:06:04,364
- No.
- No.

133
00:06:04,451 --> 00:06:07,889
She...was having trouble
with her family.

134
00:06:07,976 --> 00:06:10,195
It was her stepmother, right?

135
00:06:10,282 --> 00:06:12,110
Her natural parents are dead..

136
00:06:12,197 --> 00:06:14,678
and for some reason her
stepmother called

137
00:06:14,765 --> 00:06:16,724
a bunch of times that day.

138
00:06:16,811 --> 00:06:18,813
Did Kristin tell you
what it was about?

139
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:21,555
- No.
- No.

140
00:06:21,642 --> 00:06:23,774
No. I...I was surprised.

141
00:06:23,861 --> 00:06:26,037
I thought they were estranged.

142
00:06:44,447 --> 00:06:47,276
What was your relationship
to Kristin, Mr. Batson?

143
00:06:47,363 --> 00:06:50,105
Oh, please. Please. We know
where you're going with this.

144
00:06:50,192 --> 00:06:51,585
- Melinda--
- No.

145
00:06:51,672 --> 00:06:54,152
Let's just haul the trash
out in the open.

146
00:06:54,239 --> 00:06:56,677
You want to know if she and
Elliott were sleeping together.

147
00:06:56,764 --> 00:06:57,765
Were you?

148
00:06:57,852 --> 00:07:00,724
Never. It's a rumor.
That's all.

149
00:07:00,811 --> 00:07:03,031
Rumors usually happen
for a reason.

150
00:07:03,118 --> 00:07:04,989
- Well..
- I'll give you the reason.

151
00:07:05,076 --> 00:07:06,817
Politics.

152
00:07:06,904 --> 00:07:09,254
You want to take a female
politician down a few notches?

153
00:07:09,341 --> 00:07:11,256
Throw mud on her marriage.

154
00:07:25,836 --> 00:07:27,490
Where were you the night
Kristin was killed?

155
00:07:27,577 --> 00:07:29,187
Here. I was
on a conference call.

156
00:07:29,274 --> 00:07:31,755
With a trade delegation
from Taiwan.

157
00:07:31,842 --> 00:07:33,888
We talked until after 11:00.

158
00:07:33,975 --> 00:07:36,630
I was with him
the whole time.

159
00:07:36,717 --> 00:07:41,373
[clears throat]
We'll be married
three years this October and..

160
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:45,682
...today's news excepted, uh,
we've never been happier.

161
00:07:47,423 --> 00:07:49,381
That's hard to believe.

162
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,341
What does that mean?

163
00:07:52,428 --> 00:07:53,603
Well, there's nothing going on

164
00:07:53,690 --> 00:07:55,605
between you right now.

165
00:07:55,692 --> 00:07:57,259
Excuse me. What?

166
00:07:57,346 --> 00:08:00,480
I'm sorry. I-I meant sexually.
No heat. Right?

167
00:08:04,266 --> 00:08:06,181
I think we're done here.

168
00:08:09,314 --> 00:08:11,229
[Jane]
'You'd think a politician
would have thicker skin.'

169
00:08:11,316 --> 00:08:13,493
You accused them of lying
about their sex life

170
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:14,972
and you're surprised
they're upset?

171
00:08:15,059 --> 00:08:17,322
Oh, come on.
You're buying that happy talk?

172
00:08:17,409 --> 00:08:19,107
Really? Uh-oh.

173
00:08:19,194 --> 00:08:21,762
- Agent Minelli, sir.
- Agent Lisbon.

174
00:08:21,849 --> 00:08:23,154
I asked him down.

175
00:08:23,241 --> 00:08:25,330
Uh, Walter Crew,
Melinda Batson's dad.

176
00:08:25,417 --> 00:08:27,637
You're agents, uh,
Jane and Lisbon?

177
00:08:27,724 --> 00:08:29,204
- Yeah, we are. Hi.
- Hi.

178
00:08:29,291 --> 00:08:30,814
Sorry to track
you down like this.

179
00:08:30,901 --> 00:08:32,512
I asked Virgil here
to introduce me to the team

180
00:08:32,599 --> 00:08:35,819
handling the poor
Marley girl's case.

181
00:08:35,906 --> 00:08:39,127
Walter has been a friend
of the CBI for some time.

182
00:08:39,214 --> 00:08:42,826
He was an extremely influential
legislator for what, 20 years?

183
00:08:42,913 --> 00:08:45,089
Twenty six, but who's counting?

184
00:08:45,176 --> 00:08:47,918
Anyway, I'm old news now.

185
00:08:48,005 --> 00:08:50,617
The only thing I lobby for
is a good tee time.

186
00:08:50,704 --> 00:08:53,097
Why the interest
in the poor Marley girl's case?

187
00:08:53,184 --> 00:08:55,230
Interest? I liked her.

188
00:08:55,317 --> 00:08:57,885
Yeah, met her
in Melinda's office.

189
00:08:57,972 --> 00:09:00,844
She was good people.
Came from a tough background.

190
00:09:00,931 --> 00:09:02,585
'Didn't let that stop her.'

191
00:09:02,672 --> 00:09:04,282
I know how difficult it is
to get straight answers

192
00:09:04,369 --> 00:09:06,284
from the people
in that building there.

193
00:09:06,371 --> 00:09:09,418
If you have any problems,
you just let me know.

194
00:09:09,505 --> 00:09:11,986
- I can still knock heads.
- Oh, we'll be fine.

195
00:09:12,073 --> 00:09:13,814
Just let me know.

196
00:09:13,901 --> 00:09:15,946
- Virgil.
- Walter.

197
00:09:16,033 --> 00:09:17,644
- Take care.
- 'Sir.'

198
00:09:20,298 --> 00:09:23,563
I hate walks, Lisbon. I know
they're healthy. I don't care.

199
00:09:23,650 --> 00:09:25,434
Put me in a chair,
I'm a happy man.

200
00:09:25,521 --> 00:09:27,218
But when Walter Crew
asked me to stroll with him

201
00:09:27,305 --> 00:09:29,786
down to the Capitol,
I say, "Of course, Walter."

202
00:09:29,873 --> 00:09:31,483
- You get my drift?
- I do.

203
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:34,399
Step carefully.
I want daily reports.

204
00:09:34,486 --> 00:09:36,401
Oh, and, uh, how did
the Batson interview go?

205
00:09:36,488 --> 00:09:39,187
- Oh, that was very exciting.
- What did he do?

206
00:09:39,274 --> 00:09:41,319
Nothing that can't be repaired.

207
00:10:00,469 --> 00:10:02,471
[Carmen]
'Teresa, nice of you
to drop by.'

208
00:10:02,558 --> 00:10:04,342
I know I'm late. I'm sorry.

209
00:10:04,429 --> 00:10:06,693
Late is an interesting word
in this context.

210
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:08,912
You were
supposed to be here..

211
00:10:08,999 --> 00:10:10,871
...forty two minutes ago.

212
00:10:10,958 --> 00:10:12,568
I know. The point is,
I'm here now.

213
00:10:12,655 --> 00:10:14,918
We're supposed to talk,
so let's talk.

214
00:10:15,005 --> 00:10:17,138
I have another patient
scheduled in eight minutes.

215
00:10:17,225 --> 00:10:18,618
I can talk fast.

216
00:10:21,229 --> 00:10:23,231
This is the third time
you've been late.

217
00:10:23,318 --> 00:10:26,626
What can I say?
Lot of people getting killed.

218
00:10:26,713 --> 00:10:28,628
Can I get a coffee?

219
00:10:30,064 --> 00:10:31,195
[sighs]

220
00:10:34,155 --> 00:10:37,419
Do you know why
counseling is mandatory

221
00:10:37,506 --> 00:10:40,074
for CBI agents who've been
involved in a shooting?

222
00:10:40,161 --> 00:10:43,468
Because nobody would come
if it was voluntary?

223
00:10:43,555 --> 00:10:45,949
And that's why
it remains mandatory..

224
00:10:46,036 --> 00:10:48,996
...until I sign
and file this form.

225
00:10:53,435 --> 00:10:55,524
- See you next week.
- This is unnecessary.

226
00:10:55,611 --> 00:10:57,700
I'm fine.
I'm not traumatized.

227
00:10:57,787 --> 00:11:00,050
A man pointed a gun at you.

228
00:11:00,137 --> 00:11:01,704
A man who intended
to kill you.

229
00:11:01,791 --> 00:11:03,401
Fortunately,
Jane shot him first.

230
00:11:03,488 --> 00:11:05,186
It doesn't matter.

231
00:11:05,273 --> 00:11:08,145
You went from thinking
you were going to be killed..

232
00:11:08,232 --> 00:11:09,930
'...to watching a man die.'

233
00:11:10,017 --> 00:11:12,584
Two of the most wrenching
experiences we can have.

234
00:11:12,672 --> 00:11:13,934
And you went
through them in seconds.

235
00:11:14,021 --> 00:11:15,500
You don't think
that affected you?

236
00:11:15,587 --> 00:11:17,546
No.

237
00:11:17,633 --> 00:11:21,071
You really want to keep
seeing me, don't you?

238
00:11:21,158 --> 00:11:23,465
Next week...on time.

239
00:11:26,424 --> 00:11:27,599
Fine.

240
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:37,784
Wow.

241
00:11:37,871 --> 00:11:39,699
There's a stain on the ceiling
that looks like Elvis

242
00:11:39,786 --> 00:11:43,528
but today it looks
more like a...basset hound.

243
00:11:43,615 --> 00:11:45,792
Someone call the media.
It's a miracle.

244
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:47,576
Or maybe
someone's moved my couch.

245
00:11:47,663 --> 00:11:49,839
Cho.

246
00:11:49,926 --> 00:11:51,406
Did you move my couch?

247
00:11:51,493 --> 00:11:53,843
No. Why would I?

248
00:11:53,930 --> 00:11:56,193
Excuse me.

249
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:58,369
Did you move the couch?

250
00:11:58,456 --> 00:12:01,111
[foreign accent]
I had to, uh,
change a light. Problem?

251
00:12:01,198 --> 00:12:03,548
No, no, no. Can you help me
move it back, please?

252
00:12:08,249 --> 00:12:10,468
I got a thing, I...thanks.

253
00:12:10,555 --> 00:12:14,255
Just up there.
I think it's this way.

254
00:12:14,342 --> 00:12:15,735
Just a little.

255
00:12:17,519 --> 00:12:19,390
[grunts]
That's it.
Let me just try..

256
00:12:21,958 --> 00:12:23,394
Perfect. Thank you.

257
00:12:23,481 --> 00:12:25,788
Elvis is back.

258
00:12:25,875 --> 00:12:27,659
Anything on the stepmom?

259
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:29,400
Her name is Charlotte McAdoo.

260
00:12:29,487 --> 00:12:31,054
She called Kristin 11 times

261
00:12:31,141 --> 00:12:32,795
in the two days
before she disappeared.

262
00:12:32,882 --> 00:12:34,231
Any idea what that was about?

263
00:12:34,318 --> 00:12:35,537
No, but her son Harlan
had been picked up

264
00:12:35,624 --> 00:12:36,886
on a carjacking charge.

265
00:12:36,973 --> 00:12:38,540
He posted bail
the day Kristin disappeared.

266
00:12:38,627 --> 00:12:40,150
'Claimed he had nothing
to do with the carjacking.'

267
00:12:40,237 --> 00:12:41,761
'Said he was with Kristin
when it happened.'

268
00:12:41,848 --> 00:12:44,807
He used Kristin as his alibi?
How bad is Harlan?

269
00:12:44,894 --> 00:12:46,940
Well, mostly car theft,
some assault.

270
00:12:47,027 --> 00:12:48,332
What did Charlotte
have to say about that?

271
00:12:48,419 --> 00:12:49,812
She won't answer her phone,
won't call back.

272
00:12:49,899 --> 00:12:52,075
We're heading out
to talk to her.

273
00:12:52,162 --> 00:12:54,208
Shouldn't we be looking
for Kristin's lover?

274
00:12:54,295 --> 00:12:56,340
Who? Elliott Batson's alibi
checked out

275
00:12:56,427 --> 00:12:58,734
and there's no sign
she was seeing someone else.

276
00:12:58,821 --> 00:13:01,345
- 'We've checked.'
- Well, not enough.

277
00:13:01,432 --> 00:13:02,651
She was an immature romantic

278
00:13:02,738 --> 00:13:05,175
looking for escape
and adventure.

279
00:13:05,262 --> 00:13:06,481
She was having an affair.

280
00:13:06,568 --> 00:13:08,831
We searched
her place thoroughly.

281
00:13:08,918 --> 00:13:10,050
She kept the affair well hidden.

282
00:13:10,137 --> 00:13:11,878
Well, of course.

283
00:13:11,965 --> 00:13:15,446
It's an adventure
because it's a secret.

284
00:13:15,533 --> 00:13:18,580
But I expect
she'll tell us who it was.

285
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,669
I'll bite. How?

286
00:13:20,756 --> 00:13:22,671
[clears throat]
Check this out.

287
00:13:23,846 --> 00:13:25,195
She was a collector.

288
00:13:25,282 --> 00:13:28,459
She kept sand from every
beach she ever went to.

289
00:13:28,546 --> 00:13:31,375
She would have kept a memento
of her lover, something small.

290
00:13:31,462 --> 00:13:33,769
I bet she kept it in
a fancy jewelry box

291
00:13:33,856 --> 00:13:35,815
the kind with a figurine
on the lid.

292
00:13:35,902 --> 00:13:38,208
There was a fancy jewelry box
like that in her bedroom.

293
00:13:38,295 --> 00:13:40,689
- A ballerina.
- Ballerina. She's the type.

294
00:13:40,776 --> 00:13:42,822
But we checked it. There's
nothing in it but cheap jewelry.

295
00:13:42,909 --> 00:13:45,302
Did you check
in the secret compartment?

296
00:13:45,389 --> 00:13:46,956
The secret compartment
either on the bottom

297
00:13:47,043 --> 00:13:50,264
or one of the sides.
They usually have one.

298
00:13:50,351 --> 00:13:52,222
It's worth taking a look.

299
00:13:52,309 --> 00:13:53,441
Fine.

300
00:13:58,446 --> 00:13:59,882
Forget about Bosco.

301
00:14:03,973 --> 00:14:05,235
[Jane]
'He's got something.'

302
00:14:05,322 --> 00:14:06,976
Yeah, he's got Red John,
and we don't.

303
00:14:07,063 --> 00:14:10,240
No. No, he's got something new
on the case. New evidence.

304
00:14:10,327 --> 00:14:12,068
How can you tell?

305
00:14:12,155 --> 00:14:13,983
It's clear as can be.
I'll be right back.

306
00:14:14,070 --> 00:14:16,333
Jane, Red John
belongs to Bosco now.

307
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:18,727
I don't like it either, but
you'll have to deal with it.

308
00:14:18,814 --> 00:14:22,470
Do you want a coffee?
I'm gonna bring you a coffee.

309
00:14:28,215 --> 00:14:31,479
I need copies of each of these
sent over to division.

310
00:14:31,566 --> 00:14:33,220
'What's he doing in there?'

311
00:14:33,307 --> 00:14:34,743
He said you told him
to wait in there.

312
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:36,919
[sighs]
We'll finish later.

313
00:14:39,182 --> 00:14:41,706
- Get away from my desk.
- Where'dyougo?

314
00:14:41,793 --> 00:14:43,012
I've been here
almost half an hour.

315
00:14:43,099 --> 00:14:45,145
And stop hacking my passcodes

316
00:14:45,232 --> 00:14:46,581
and stop hustling my people.

317
00:14:46,668 --> 00:14:48,409
It's not doing you
any good, you know.

318
00:14:48,496 --> 00:14:50,541
I don't know
what you're talking about.

319
00:14:50,628 --> 00:14:53,022
What'd you get on Red John?

320
00:14:53,109 --> 00:14:54,806
And what makes you think
I got anything?

321
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,417
Folder.

322
00:14:56,504 --> 00:14:59,246
You moved it
when you saw me, protected it.

323
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:01,988
It's the one thing
you'd protect from me.

324
00:15:02,075 --> 00:15:03,990
It's the cover-up
that gave you away.

325
00:15:04,077 --> 00:15:05,948
- Huh.
- What is it?

326
00:15:06,035 --> 00:15:10,561
It's none
of your business, so go.

327
00:15:10,648 --> 00:15:12,781
You need
to understand something.

328
00:15:12,868 --> 00:15:15,566
Red John doesn't make mistakes.
He doesn't leave clues.

329
00:15:15,653 --> 00:15:18,265
If you have new evidence, it's
because he wants you to have it.

330
00:15:18,352 --> 00:15:19,919
The question
isn't what does it mean?

331
00:15:20,006 --> 00:15:21,921
It's why did he give it to you?

332
00:15:22,008 --> 00:15:23,183
That's deep.

333
00:15:23,270 --> 00:15:25,402
Tell me what it is.
I can help you.

334
00:15:25,489 --> 00:15:26,882
Have you ever seen
a crack addict

335
00:15:26,969 --> 00:15:28,536
when they're begging for a hit?

336
00:15:28,623 --> 00:15:30,668
You got that same look
in your eye that they get.

337
00:15:30,755 --> 00:15:33,584
Oh. You've got me
all figured out.

338
00:15:33,671 --> 00:15:35,717
[cell phone rings]

339
00:15:35,804 --> 00:15:37,762
Hey, Van Pelt.
Did you get it?

340
00:15:37,849 --> 00:15:40,330
There's a secret compartment,
just like you said.

341
00:15:40,417 --> 00:15:43,855
- And what was in it?
- Nothing. It's empty.

342
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:45,988
Huh...alright.

343
00:15:48,556 --> 00:15:50,166
Bad news, huh?

344
00:15:50,253 --> 00:15:52,212
No, not at all.

345
00:15:52,299 --> 00:15:55,650
It's like you said, it's
the cover-up that gave you away.

346
00:15:55,737 --> 00:15:59,001
You're an addict, Jane.
You need help.

347
00:15:59,088 --> 00:16:02,004
- You're making a mistake.
- You can go.

348
00:16:14,843 --> 00:16:15,800
[Rigsby]
I got tickets to the Kings game
tomorrow night. You wanna go?

349
00:16:15,887 --> 00:16:17,628
- I'm going out.
- Who with?

350
00:16:17,715 --> 00:16:19,935
The niece of that shopkeeper
we met on that Red John thing.

351
00:16:20,022 --> 00:16:23,939
Oh, finally.
Took you long enough.

352
00:16:24,809 --> 00:16:26,376
- 5B?
- Yeah.

353
00:16:26,463 --> 00:16:28,030
Well, we talked on the phone.
She's nice.

354
00:16:28,117 --> 00:16:31,120
- We'll see how it goes.
- I expect a full report.

355
00:16:31,207 --> 00:16:33,775
- In your dreams.
- Hey, I got you that number.

356
00:16:33,862 --> 00:16:35,820
- You owe me.
- No.

357
00:16:37,692 --> 00:16:39,999
- Charlotte McAdoo?
- Yeah.

358
00:16:40,086 --> 00:16:41,304
We need to talk to you
about your stepdaughter

359
00:16:41,391 --> 00:16:42,523
Kristin Marley.

360
00:16:49,051 --> 00:16:51,575
You know that Kristin's dead,
right, Charlotte?

361
00:16:51,662 --> 00:16:52,924
What about it?

362
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:55,188
I guess
you're pretty broken up.

363
00:16:55,275 --> 00:16:58,582
She wasn't my kid. I'm not
the huggy type. Sue me.

364
00:16:58,669 --> 00:17:00,280
If you didn't like Kristin
why'd you make all those calls

365
00:17:00,367 --> 00:17:02,630
right before she disappeared?

366
00:17:02,717 --> 00:17:05,589
- Don't remember.
- It was a week ago.

367
00:17:05,676 --> 00:17:08,331
I'm old.
My memory's bad.

368
00:17:08,418 --> 00:17:09,680
Did it have something to do
with your son Harlan?

369
00:17:09,767 --> 00:17:11,465
What about Harlan?

370
00:17:11,552 --> 00:17:13,945
He used Kristin as an alibi
when he was arrested.

371
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,382
But Kristin told Sacramento PD

372
00:17:15,469 --> 00:17:17,558
she hadn't seen Harlan
for months.

373
00:17:17,645 --> 00:17:19,038
Were you asking Kristin
to change her story

374
00:17:19,125 --> 00:17:20,778
and lie an alibi
for her stepbrother?

375
00:17:20,865 --> 00:17:22,345
No, that's crazy.

376
00:17:22,432 --> 00:17:24,260
- Where is Harlan?
- 'I don't know.

377
00:17:24,347 --> 00:17:26,436
'I haven't seen him for days.'

378
00:17:26,523 --> 00:17:29,961
Okay. Thanks for your time.

379
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,746
That's...that's it?

380
00:17:31,833 --> 00:17:33,835
We'll see ourselves out.
Thank you.

381
00:17:42,322 --> 00:17:43,932
[whispers]
You think Charlotte
smokes filtered and unfiltered?

382
00:17:44,019 --> 00:17:45,803
Not if she's got a visitor.
Bathroom or closet?

383
00:17:45,890 --> 00:17:47,327
- Bathroom.
- I think closet.

384
00:17:47,414 --> 00:17:48,937
- You wanna bet?
- What do I get if I win?

385
00:17:49,024 --> 00:17:50,243
I pay for lunch next week.

386
00:17:50,330 --> 00:17:52,245
I win, you tell me
about your date.

387
00:17:52,332 --> 00:17:53,855
That's enough time.

388
00:17:55,291 --> 00:17:57,598
- Hey, Harlan.
- Oh, crap.

389
00:17:57,685 --> 00:17:59,991
Harlan, were you
in the bathroom or the closet?

390
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,602
- Closet. Wh--
- I told you.

391
00:18:01,689 --> 00:18:03,908
- We didn't bet.
- Yes, we did.

392
00:18:08,522 --> 00:18:11,002
No law against
being in a closet.

393
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:12,961
No, Harlan, but it is
kinda suspicious.

394
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:19,663
- You got no right to hold me.
- We're just talking.

395
00:18:22,797 --> 00:18:24,320
Alright, what do you
want to talk about?

396
00:18:24,407 --> 00:18:27,889
Kristin Marley,
when did you see her last?

397
00:18:27,976 --> 00:18:30,065
- What happened to her?
- You tell us.

398
00:18:30,152 --> 00:18:32,676
Well, I got nothing to say
about her.

399
00:18:32,763 --> 00:18:34,200
You must be mad that
she didn't back your alibi

400
00:18:34,287 --> 00:18:36,419
on the carjacking charge, huh?

401
00:18:36,506 --> 00:18:40,815
First of all...that arrest
was completely bogus.

402
00:18:40,902 --> 00:18:42,991
And, B, that stuck-up bitch
don't get

403
00:18:43,078 --> 00:18:44,514
what the word family means, so..

404
00:18:44,601 --> 00:18:45,863
What is that?

405
00:18:45,950 --> 00:18:48,214
Family's supposed to help
when you're down.

406
00:18:48,301 --> 00:18:49,737
But she gets a job
in the Capitol

407
00:18:49,824 --> 00:18:51,521
with some big money friends,
and pow

408
00:18:51,608 --> 00:18:54,220
she's too good
for the people she grew up with.

409
00:18:54,307 --> 00:18:57,092
She don't get what the word
family is all about, you know?

410
00:18:57,179 --> 00:19:00,965
Didn't. She's dead.

411
00:19:01,052 --> 00:19:03,011
Yeah.

412
00:19:03,098 --> 00:19:06,101
That's too bad.

413
00:19:06,188 --> 00:19:07,972
Did you have
any contact with Kristin

414
00:19:08,059 --> 00:19:09,496
after you posted bail, Harlan?

415
00:19:09,583 --> 00:19:10,975
- No.
- None?

416
00:19:11,062 --> 00:19:12,368
That's what I said.

417
00:19:12,455 --> 00:19:13,804
It's funny,
'cause our tech guys

418
00:19:13,891 --> 00:19:15,066
have been going through
her cell phone.

419
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:17,678
There's some deleted
texts on it.

420
00:19:17,765 --> 00:19:20,594
Four of them were from you
the day she disappeared.

421
00:19:20,681 --> 00:19:24,946
Well, that's what you call
a-a glitch, computer thing.

422
00:19:25,033 --> 00:19:28,036
You were threatening Kristin to
get her to lie for you, right?

423
00:19:28,123 --> 00:19:31,387
- Didn't say that.
- I could see why you'd do it.

424
00:19:31,474 --> 00:19:33,433
You're facing serious time.

425
00:19:34,825 --> 00:19:38,351
You arresting me?

426
00:19:38,438 --> 00:19:39,830
You got no right
to hold me if you ain't.

427
00:19:39,917 --> 00:19:41,876
You're not under arrest.

428
00:19:41,963 --> 00:19:43,704
But you are out on bail,
and that can be revoked

429
00:19:43,791 --> 00:19:46,359
if the judge thinks
you're not being cooperative.

430
00:19:46,446 --> 00:19:48,448
Do you want a soda, Harlan?

431
00:19:50,754 --> 00:19:52,321
I want chips.

432
00:19:56,717 --> 00:20:00,024
If he took Kristin's body to the
bridge, he put her in his trunk.

433
00:20:00,111 --> 00:20:02,026
It's worth taking a look.
I'll call the district attorney.

434
00:20:02,113 --> 00:20:03,593
If Harlan hears
we're looking at his car

435
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:07,162
he'll be out the door before
the warrant comes through.

436
00:20:07,249 --> 00:20:08,729
We're gonna make him
want to stay.

437
00:20:08,816 --> 00:20:10,209
'Van Pelt.'

438
00:20:12,994 --> 00:20:14,952
You're taking over
the McAdoo interview.

439
00:20:15,039 --> 00:20:18,304
I'm totally ready for that. I
can get him to confess to this.

440
00:20:18,391 --> 00:20:20,044
Yeah, maybe.

441
00:20:20,131 --> 00:20:22,090
The main thing is, you keep
him in there long enough

442
00:20:22,177 --> 00:20:24,527
for us to search his car.
Be friendly.

443
00:20:24,614 --> 00:20:27,095
He thinks he's a player.
He'll eat it up.

444
00:20:27,182 --> 00:20:29,010
What do you mean,
be friendly?

445
00:20:29,097 --> 00:20:30,620
Need a map?

446
00:20:31,534 --> 00:20:33,014
Good luck.

447
00:20:41,457 --> 00:20:44,765
Hey...I heard Bosco cleaned
your clock this morning.

448
00:20:44,852 --> 00:20:47,898
Well, that's one interpretation.

449
00:20:47,985 --> 00:20:51,293
I get it. It's tough to have
Red John taken away like that.

450
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:52,729
Bet you'd give a lot
to know

451
00:20:52,816 --> 00:20:54,775
what they're saying
in Bosco's office.

452
00:20:57,299 --> 00:20:58,431
Yeah.

453
00:21:01,521 --> 00:21:03,131
Yeah, I would.

454
00:21:03,218 --> 00:21:04,828
You gotta let it go, man.

455
00:21:04,915 --> 00:21:06,569
Forget about the jewelry box.
You missed one.

456
00:21:06,656 --> 00:21:09,006
- So what?
- Actually, I didn't.

457
00:21:09,093 --> 00:21:12,009
I'm pursuing an independent
line of investigation.

458
00:21:12,096 --> 00:21:14,925
Gonna crack
this case in 24 hours.

459
00:21:15,012 --> 00:21:17,667
I think we might be
ahead of you this time.

460
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,770
Hi, Harlan.

461
00:21:33,857 --> 00:21:35,729
I'm agent Van Pelt.

462
00:21:35,816 --> 00:21:39,428
Special agent Lisbon asked me
to take over the interview.

463
00:21:39,515 --> 00:21:40,560
Why?

464
00:21:40,647 --> 00:21:43,084
She's busy
with something else.

465
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:50,309
So I've looked through
your file and it's, uh..

466
00:21:50,396 --> 00:21:53,050
...it's very..

467
00:21:53,137 --> 00:21:54,574
What?

468
00:21:54,661 --> 00:21:56,793
Well..

469
00:21:56,880 --> 00:22:00,449
I don't think you had
anything to do with this crime.

470
00:22:00,536 --> 00:22:03,191
Thank you.
That's what I've been saying.

471
00:22:03,278 --> 00:22:05,454
It's just a big
misunderstanding, I'm sure.

472
00:22:05,541 --> 00:22:08,022
Yeah. You got that right.

473
00:22:08,109 --> 00:22:12,896
But let's fill out the forms,
so everyone's happy, okay?

474
00:22:12,983 --> 00:22:14,724
Mmm. Chips.

475
00:22:15,725 --> 00:22:16,857
[crunching]

476
00:22:18,641 --> 00:22:21,252
So...let's make a time line

477
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,864
of everywhere you've been
since Kristin disappeared.

478
00:22:23,951 --> 00:22:25,126
Okay.

479
00:22:27,171 --> 00:22:29,217
- You want another?
- Mm.

480
00:22:51,021 --> 00:22:53,415
[doorbell rings]

481
00:22:58,551 --> 00:23:00,204
[Jane]
'These all pictures
of your daughter?'

482
00:23:00,291 --> 00:23:01,989
[Walter]
'Yes, they are.'

483
00:23:02,076 --> 00:23:03,120
[Jane]
'Well, it's surprising
there's not more'

484
00:23:03,207 --> 00:23:05,296
'pictures of you.'

485
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:07,037
Given your standing, that is.

486
00:23:07,124 --> 00:23:09,866
What, me talking
to a bunch of famous windbags?

487
00:23:09,953 --> 00:23:12,739
Had those. Took 'em down.
Waste of space.

488
00:23:12,826 --> 00:23:15,263
- Thank you.
- No, my days are over.

489
00:23:15,350 --> 00:23:18,048
Melinda has got the future.

490
00:23:18,135 --> 00:23:21,487
She could go far, very far,
if she listens to me.

491
00:23:21,574 --> 00:23:24,446
Now what did you want
to talk about?

492
00:23:26,535 --> 00:23:27,667
[sighs]

493
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:31,105
How long were you sleeping
with Kristin Marley

494
00:23:31,192 --> 00:23:33,281
before she was killed?

495
00:23:33,368 --> 00:23:36,632
[scoffs]
What makes you think I was?

496
00:23:36,719 --> 00:23:39,461
You're a politician.
Ambitious. Narcissistic.

497
00:23:39,548 --> 00:23:41,071
Addicted to the love
of strangers.

498
00:23:41,158 --> 00:23:43,117
She was beautiful,
impressionable

499
00:23:43,204 --> 00:23:45,641
no doubt flattered
by your attentions.

500
00:23:45,728 --> 00:23:46,990
And you're not
the sort of man

501
00:23:47,077 --> 00:23:50,472
to deny yourself
an object of desire.

502
00:23:50,559 --> 00:23:52,648
I'm married 38 years, Mr. Jane.

503
00:23:52,735 --> 00:23:54,041
[chuckles]

504
00:23:54,128 --> 00:23:56,304
As I said.

505
00:23:56,391 --> 00:23:58,872
Uh, even if
what you say is true

506
00:23:58,959 --> 00:24:02,136
and I'm not saying it is

507
00:24:02,223 --> 00:24:05,835
what does that have to do
with poor Kristin's murder?

508
00:24:05,922 --> 00:24:08,055
Blackmail or something like it.

509
00:24:10,144 --> 00:24:13,060
The business adultery leads to.

510
00:24:13,147 --> 00:24:17,412
Ah...but...even if I am

511
00:24:17,499 --> 00:24:20,241
what you say I am and..

512
00:24:20,328 --> 00:24:22,112
...I'm not saying I am..

513
00:24:22,199 --> 00:24:24,898
...wouldn't I have faced
a situation like this before..

514
00:24:24,985 --> 00:24:28,075
...and handled it
without killing anybody?

515
00:24:28,162 --> 00:24:29,598
- It's a good point.
- 'Mm.'

516
00:24:29,685 --> 00:24:32,253
- I'll think about that.
- Please.

517
00:24:33,515 --> 00:24:35,038
Mm.

518
00:24:35,125 --> 00:24:37,171
Anything else?

519
00:24:37,258 --> 00:24:39,216
What? Mm? Sorry?

520
00:24:39,303 --> 00:24:42,306
Well, whoever it is, I'll have
the killer by the morning.

521
00:24:42,393 --> 00:24:44,874
So, uh, you should act
accordingly.

522
00:24:44,961 --> 00:24:46,963
- Thank you for your time.
- You're welcome.

523
00:24:48,399 --> 00:24:50,793
[instrumental music]

524
00:24:52,795 --> 00:24:55,537
[Cho]
You think Harlan
ever cleans out his car?

525
00:24:55,624 --> 00:24:57,670
So where you taking the
shopkeeper's niece for dinner?

526
00:24:57,757 --> 00:24:58,845
I'd rather not talk about it.

527
00:24:58,932 --> 00:25:00,716
- Why not?
- It's private.

528
00:25:00,803 --> 00:25:02,849
Oh, come on.

529
00:25:02,936 --> 00:25:05,329
Let's talk about somethin' else.

530
00:25:05,416 --> 00:25:06,722
I'll call technical services.

531
00:25:06,809 --> 00:25:08,158
They can pop that lock
in 20 seconds.

532
00:25:08,245 --> 00:25:09,551
It'll take 'em
two hours to get here.

533
00:25:09,638 --> 00:25:10,813
It took you two hours
to open the door

534
00:25:10,900 --> 00:25:11,858
last time you tried this
and we had to pay

535
00:25:11,945 --> 00:25:12,859
for the busted window.

536
00:25:12,946 --> 00:25:15,165
Fluke.

537
00:25:15,252 --> 00:25:16,732
If I had a date,
I'd tell you about it.

538
00:25:16,819 --> 00:25:18,342
[scoffs]
Yeah.

539
00:25:18,429 --> 00:25:20,344
I would tell you anything
you wanted to know.

540
00:25:20,431 --> 00:25:23,870
Okay, you ever gonna man up
and make a move on Van Pelt?

541
00:25:23,957 --> 00:25:26,350
- Fine. Don't tell me.
- Right.

542
00:25:31,791 --> 00:25:32,922
[grunts]

543
00:25:40,800 --> 00:25:42,497
Hey. Check this out.

544
00:25:42,584 --> 00:25:45,152
Wasn't the other one of these
on Kristin Marley's foot?

545
00:25:45,239 --> 00:25:46,588
I'll call Lisbon.

546
00:25:52,855 --> 00:25:54,988
Kristin's shoe was
in your trunk.

547
00:25:55,075 --> 00:25:58,295
No. No way.
Uh-uh.

548
00:25:58,382 --> 00:26:00,559
You want to tell us
how it got there, Harlan?

549
00:26:00,646 --> 00:26:03,170
I don't know.
Maybe you put it there, huh?

550
00:26:03,257 --> 00:26:06,303
You have no alibi for the night
of Kristin's disappearance.

551
00:26:06,390 --> 00:26:08,523
I told you.
I was with my mom.

552
00:26:08,610 --> 00:26:11,526
She was concealing you
when we went to pick you up.

553
00:26:11,613 --> 00:26:13,572
- It's not gonna cut it.
- You were mad at Kristin.

554
00:26:13,659 --> 00:26:15,443
- A little, but--
- You threatened her.

555
00:26:15,530 --> 00:26:16,662
No.

556
00:26:19,447 --> 00:26:21,318
Okay, I mean, a-a little,
but come on.

557
00:26:21,405 --> 00:26:23,799
I-I wouldn't hurt her for real.

558
00:26:23,886 --> 00:26:27,150
That's not much
of a story, Harlan.

559
00:26:27,237 --> 00:26:28,978
[whispers]
I thought you believed me.

560
00:26:29,065 --> 00:26:31,851
You were wrong.

561
00:26:31,938 --> 00:26:34,593
[chuckles]
You know what? The hell
with this. I'm outta here.

562
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:35,942
Not quite yet.

563
00:26:36,029 --> 00:26:39,728
- Oh, you're gonna stop me?
- Yeah.

564
00:26:39,815 --> 00:26:41,295
- Did you make the arrest?
- I did.

565
00:26:41,382 --> 00:26:43,819
Ah, victory is yours.

566
00:26:43,906 --> 00:26:45,212
Yes, it is.

567
00:26:47,649 --> 00:26:48,824
What?

568
00:26:48,911 --> 00:26:50,043
Oh, nothing.

569
00:26:50,130 --> 00:26:52,828
- Come on.
- No. No.

570
00:26:52,915 --> 00:26:54,221
I'm still waiting.

571
00:26:57,354 --> 00:26:59,530
Throwing the body off
the bridge was a smart move.

572
00:26:59,618 --> 00:27:04,057
Good chance the coroner
would declare it a suicide.

573
00:27:04,144 --> 00:27:05,362
Do you really think
Harlan McAdoo

574
00:27:05,449 --> 00:27:06,929
would come up with that?

575
00:27:07,016 --> 00:27:09,279
Dumb people can come up
with smart ideas

576
00:27:09,366 --> 00:27:11,804
and smart people
can come up with dumb ones.

577
00:27:11,891 --> 00:27:13,588
Eh, true.

578
00:27:15,503 --> 00:27:17,897
I'll have the real killer
here in 12 hours or so.

579
00:27:17,984 --> 00:27:20,464
- What are you talking about?
- You'll see. Bye.

580
00:27:20,551 --> 00:27:21,552
Jane.

581
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:22,553
Hey, boss, you want me to send

582
00:27:22,641 --> 00:27:25,774
McAdoo down to be arraigned?

583
00:27:25,861 --> 00:27:27,036
Not yet. Sit on him.

584
00:27:27,123 --> 00:27:28,385
See if he comes up
with something useful

585
00:27:28,472 --> 00:27:30,039
once he calms down.

586
00:27:34,174 --> 00:27:35,784
Well, obviously,
you've got to get it out of

587
00:27:35,871 --> 00:27:37,351
committee before..

588
00:27:37,438 --> 00:27:40,746
- Mr. Jane.
- Hi. Don't mind me.

589
00:27:40,833 --> 00:27:42,617
What are you doing?

590
00:27:42,704 --> 00:27:46,447
- Hard at work, on the case.
- I don't understand.

591
00:27:46,534 --> 00:27:49,102
We got a call from agent Minelli
saying that an arrest

592
00:27:49,189 --> 00:27:50,799
had been made,
Kristin's stepbrother.

593
00:27:50,886 --> 00:27:54,237
Nope, nope, nope. Wrong guy.

594
00:27:54,324 --> 00:27:56,239
How can that be?

595
00:27:56,326 --> 00:27:59,982
Simple miscarriage of justice,
happens all the time.

596
00:28:00,069 --> 00:28:01,244
What does that mean?

597
00:28:01,331 --> 00:28:04,030
It means I have to find
the real killer.

598
00:28:04,117 --> 00:28:06,336
The real killer? How?

599
00:28:06,423 --> 00:28:08,077
Oh, Kristin was a collector.

600
00:28:08,164 --> 00:28:12,995
Ergo, the identity of Kristin's
killer will be in her things.

601
00:28:13,082 --> 00:28:14,257
How can you be sure
it's there?

602
00:28:14,344 --> 00:28:15,781
Oh, I'm sure.

603
00:28:15,868 --> 00:28:17,434
Mr. Jane, this isn't acceptable.

604
00:28:17,521 --> 00:28:18,653
First you accost my father--

605
00:28:18,740 --> 00:28:20,089
Oh, I wouldn't use
the word accost.

606
00:28:20,176 --> 00:28:21,656
And now you're
ransacking my office.

607
00:28:21,743 --> 00:28:23,223
- Calm down, Melinda.
- I won't calm down.

608
00:28:23,310 --> 00:28:24,746
I thought
we'd put this behind us.

609
00:28:24,833 --> 00:28:26,617
Not much
of a campaign slogan.

610
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:31,144
"Batson, so tough on crime, she
puts the innocent behind bars."

611
00:28:34,147 --> 00:28:36,627
Do what you have to do.
W-we'll help in any way we can.

612
00:28:36,715 --> 00:28:39,761
Great. Thank you. There's
a couple of boxes right there.

613
00:28:39,848 --> 00:28:42,416
If you could just,
uh, grab one each

614
00:28:42,503 --> 00:28:44,418
and follow me to my car.

615
00:28:49,902 --> 00:28:52,469
[Minelli]
'Lisbon, didn't you arrest
McAdoo?'

616
00:28:52,556 --> 00:28:54,123
[Lisbon]
'Yeah, we did.'

617
00:28:54,210 --> 00:28:55,864
DA says you haven't
sent him down to be arraigned.

618
00:28:55,951 --> 00:28:57,779
We've 48 hours to do that.
We still have some loose ends.

619
00:28:57,866 --> 00:29:00,956
- What, what loose ends? Him?
- No.

620
00:29:01,043 --> 00:29:03,785
What are you doing?
No, don't tell me.

621
00:29:03,872 --> 00:29:07,441
I want this off my desk.
Get McAdoo to the DA tonight.

622
00:29:07,528 --> 00:29:10,096
How hard is Crew
leaning on you?

623
00:29:10,183 --> 00:29:11,967
- He's not.
- Then who's doing it for him?

624
00:29:12,054 --> 00:29:13,882
- No one.
- Is this my case, sir?

625
00:29:13,969 --> 00:29:15,754
Yes, but--

626
00:29:15,841 --> 00:29:17,843
Then it's my decision
as to when the suspect is

627
00:29:17,930 --> 00:29:21,020
handed over to
the District Attorney, right?

628
00:29:21,107 --> 00:29:22,761
If McAdoo isn't
in the DA's office

629
00:29:22,848 --> 00:29:24,153
first thing tomorrow morning..

630
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:26,677
...this becomes
a different conversation.

631
00:29:29,202 --> 00:29:31,595
[sighs]

632
00:29:31,682 --> 00:29:34,903
- You won't regret this.
- I already do.

633
00:29:37,079 --> 00:29:39,473
[cricket chirping]

634
00:29:58,013 --> 00:29:59,667
[phone rings]

635
00:29:59,754 --> 00:30:01,060
[Lisbon]
'Hey, this is Lisbon.'

636
00:30:01,147 --> 00:30:02,888
'Leave a message.
I'll call you back.'

637
00:30:02,975 --> 00:30:04,063
[beep]

638
00:30:04,150 --> 00:30:06,152
I found what I was looking for.

639
00:30:06,239 --> 00:30:08,023
I don't want to risk taking it
out of the office

640
00:30:08,110 --> 00:30:10,983
so I'm gonna put it in the top
right hand drawer of your desk.

641
00:30:11,070 --> 00:30:12,941
When you get this, call me.

642
00:30:22,124 --> 00:30:23,430
[door opens]

643
00:30:47,715 --> 00:30:50,587
"Ah ha."

644
00:30:50,674 --> 00:30:53,634
[foreign accent]
Oh. Y-you startled me.
Uh..

645
00:30:54,983 --> 00:30:58,682
I'll...I'll just
get out of your way.

646
00:30:58,769 --> 00:31:03,078
- Stand still. Turn around.
- Huh? Whoa. Whoa.

647
00:31:03,165 --> 00:31:04,514
What is this?

648
00:31:04,601 --> 00:31:06,647
Who are you
and who are you working for?

649
00:31:06,734 --> 00:31:11,043
I work for the building.
I clean. I clean.

650
00:31:11,130 --> 00:31:15,482
Oh, you're not a cleaner.
Look at this place. It's a mess.

651
00:31:15,569 --> 00:31:17,092
You're the fixer.

652
00:31:17,179 --> 00:31:21,140
You've been listening in
on our conversations.

653
00:31:21,227 --> 00:31:24,099
Huh? What's that? That's one
of the bugs you placed.

654
00:31:24,186 --> 00:31:26,754
I found it
in the overhead light.

655
00:31:26,841 --> 00:31:29,757
When I told Van Pelt to go
and check out the jewelry box

656
00:31:29,844 --> 00:31:31,933
you overheard
and you went there first.

657
00:31:32,020 --> 00:31:34,675
And it was you that placed
the shoe in McAdoo's trunk.

658
00:31:34,762 --> 00:31:37,808
- I'm on the cleaning crew.
- Oh, really?

659
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:40,899
I'm new.
You can call my supervisor.

660
00:31:40,986 --> 00:31:42,465
'Marty, uh..'

661
00:31:42,552 --> 00:31:45,468
Marty, uh, Toretta, huh?

662
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:49,124
- Call him up right now.
- No.

663
00:31:49,211 --> 00:31:50,778
Wake him up.

664
00:31:53,607 --> 00:31:56,305
I got no idea
what you're talking about here.

665
00:31:56,392 --> 00:31:58,046
We're talking about
accessory to murder

666
00:31:58,133 --> 00:32:00,396
conspiracy, obstruction.

667
00:32:00,483 --> 00:32:02,268
'Who hired you?'

668
00:32:02,355 --> 00:32:04,835
Murder?

669
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:07,316
Oh, I-I don't feel too good.

670
00:32:07,403 --> 00:32:09,753
- Can I sit? Can I--
- Oh, take a seat.

671
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:10,972
Thanks.

672
00:32:13,583 --> 00:32:15,368
[American accent]
Alright. Oh, no, no. No.

673
00:32:15,455 --> 00:32:18,849
- Calm. Are you calm?
- Sure.

674
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:23,724
Alright, now, I want you
to lift your gun out

675
00:32:23,811 --> 00:32:26,770
with two fingers
and slide it across the floor.

676
00:32:34,082 --> 00:32:35,823
Now, get your cuffs.

677
00:32:35,910 --> 00:32:37,825
This isn't gonna work.

678
00:32:39,348 --> 00:32:41,916
The door.
Hook yourself up.

679
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:51,491
Toss the keys.

680
00:32:53,623 --> 00:32:55,582
[keys jingle]

681
00:32:55,669 --> 00:32:59,673
Now you and I are
gonna walk out here.

682
00:32:59,760 --> 00:33:01,631
Sure.

683
00:33:01,718 --> 00:33:03,851
It's a little stroll.

684
00:33:03,938 --> 00:33:06,288
[indistinct radio chatter,
door opens]

685
00:33:10,031 --> 00:33:11,337
[door squeaking]

686
00:33:16,603 --> 00:33:18,779
Find out where he goes.

687
00:33:18,866 --> 00:33:21,695
- Uh, no, I think--
- Go, now. Go.

688
00:33:22,565 --> 00:33:23,740
Oh.

689
00:33:25,133 --> 00:33:27,396
- Ma'am.
- Keys, please.

690
00:33:27,483 --> 00:33:29,007
There. Yeah.

691
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:43,282
[tires screeching]

692
00:33:54,293 --> 00:33:56,686
[intense music]

693
00:34:25,759 --> 00:34:27,065
[footsteps approaching]

694
00:34:29,806 --> 00:34:34,202
So, Agent Lisbon, here we are.

695
00:34:34,289 --> 00:34:36,465
What's this about?

696
00:34:36,552 --> 00:34:38,380
This is Art Cavalleri.

697
00:34:38,467 --> 00:34:40,643
He's the private investigator
one of you hired

698
00:34:40,730 --> 00:34:42,906
to wiretap and obstruct
our investigation.

699
00:34:42,993 --> 00:34:44,343
Really?

700
00:34:44,430 --> 00:34:46,867
He's agreed to talk in exchange
for leniency.

701
00:34:46,954 --> 00:34:49,261
'I called you down here
to offer you the same deal.'

702
00:34:49,348 --> 00:34:51,306
Well, that's very nice of you.

703
00:34:51,393 --> 00:34:52,786
You can discuss it
with my attorney.

704
00:34:52,873 --> 00:34:54,657
- Melinda?
- I have nothing to say.

705
00:34:54,744 --> 00:34:57,530
Even if you had nothing to do
with Kristin Marley's murder..

706
00:34:57,617 --> 00:34:59,097
'...with what Cavalleri
is saying'

707
00:34:59,184 --> 00:35:00,750
'about the conspiracy
and the cover up'

708
00:35:00,837 --> 00:35:02,535
you're all gonna do
a lot of time in prison.

709
00:35:02,622 --> 00:35:05,799
- I don't need to hear anymore.
- W-wait. I-I do.

710
00:35:05,886 --> 00:35:07,453
What kind of leniency
are we talking about here?

711
00:35:07,540 --> 00:35:09,672
- Elliott.
- Depends, Mr. Batson.

712
00:35:09,759 --> 00:35:11,021
What do you know?

713
00:35:11,109 --> 00:35:12,806
I need an assurance
that any charges

714
00:35:12,893 --> 00:35:14,460
related to the murder
will be dropped.

715
00:35:14,547 --> 00:35:15,722
You got it, as long
as you didn't have

716
00:35:15,809 --> 00:35:17,071
anything to do with the murder.

717
00:35:17,158 --> 00:35:19,117
If you'll excuse us,
I want some private time

718
00:35:19,204 --> 00:35:20,640
with my family right now.

719
00:35:20,727 --> 00:35:23,164
Mr. Crew, stay there.
Go on.

720
00:35:24,948 --> 00:35:26,559
[Jane]
'Oh, come on.
Spit it out, man.'

721
00:35:26,646 --> 00:35:29,649
The marriage is a sham.
She's gay. You're the beard.

722
00:35:29,736 --> 00:35:32,217
It was kind of obvious
from the start.

723
00:35:32,304 --> 00:35:34,828
I had an arrangement
with Melinda Elliott.

724
00:35:34,915 --> 00:35:36,046
Don't.

725
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:37,222
I agreed to marry Melinda

726
00:35:37,309 --> 00:35:39,311
in exchange for..

727
00:35:39,398 --> 00:35:40,877
'...certain
financial considerations.'

728
00:35:40,964 --> 00:35:42,357
Batson, we had a deal.

729
00:35:42,444 --> 00:35:44,054
Did that deal
include time in prison?

730
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:45,665
I-I don't think so.

731
00:35:45,752 --> 00:35:47,493
So it was your own people
that started the rumor

732
00:35:47,580 --> 00:35:50,496
about you and Kristin to hide
her affair with Melinda.

733
00:35:50,583 --> 00:35:52,802
Yes.

734
00:35:52,889 --> 00:35:54,413
I'm sorry, Melinda.

735
00:35:56,458 --> 00:35:59,113
Kristin broke it off
shortly before she disappeared.

736
00:35:59,200 --> 00:36:01,811
Melinda was upset.

737
00:36:01,898 --> 00:36:05,641
And were you with Melinda
the night Kristin disappeared?

738
00:36:08,340 --> 00:36:10,994
No. I didn't see her
until late that night.

739
00:36:11,081 --> 00:36:14,389
She was...a mess.

740
00:36:14,476 --> 00:36:15,956
But she wouldn't
tell me what had happened.

741
00:36:16,043 --> 00:36:18,306
Kristin had something
hidden in her apartment.

742
00:36:18,393 --> 00:36:21,918
- A...memento, I guess.
- Lovers' memento.

743
00:36:22,005 --> 00:36:25,835
Cavalleri had found it,
but we took it out of his car.

744
00:36:25,922 --> 00:36:28,969
It could be a W,
but I think it's an M.

745
00:36:36,063 --> 00:36:39,153
'You and your father were both
having an affair with Kristin.'

746
00:36:39,240 --> 00:36:40,459
No.

747
00:36:43,244 --> 00:36:45,159
No.

748
00:36:45,246 --> 00:36:47,727
- I--
- Melinda.

749
00:36:47,814 --> 00:36:51,296
Ihad a relationship
with Kristin.

750
00:36:51,383 --> 00:36:54,124
Heseduced her.

751
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:56,475
Took her..

752
00:36:56,562 --> 00:36:58,433
...the way he's taken women
his whole life.

753
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:01,784
- I was trying to make a point.
- You were what?

754
00:37:01,871 --> 00:37:03,395
- I was trying to show you--
- What?

755
00:37:03,482 --> 00:37:04,961
That she was just another girl.

756
00:37:05,048 --> 00:37:06,876
That she was just
another trashy little girl.

757
00:37:06,963 --> 00:37:11,533
You thought you were in love,
but she was just having a fling.

758
00:37:11,620 --> 00:37:13,927
He believed that
you were giving away

759
00:37:14,014 --> 00:37:17,626
a very bright political career
because of some strumpet.

760
00:37:17,713 --> 00:37:19,933
What happened that night?

761
00:37:26,635 --> 00:37:28,463
Melinda,
every day you don't talk

762
00:37:28,550 --> 00:37:30,726
'is another day
you're on the news.'

763
00:37:36,776 --> 00:37:39,300
I knew Kristin
was seeing someone..

764
00:37:39,387 --> 00:37:42,172
...but I didn't know who it was.

765
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:45,263
So I followed her..

766
00:37:47,700 --> 00:37:50,050
...and that's when
I saw my father.

767
00:37:51,530 --> 00:37:53,009
[exhales deeply]

768
00:37:53,096 --> 00:37:56,752
After he left,
I went into her apartment.

769
00:38:01,931 --> 00:38:04,064
She had these stone bookends.

770
00:38:05,674 --> 00:38:06,980
'I grabbed one.'

771
00:38:11,289 --> 00:38:14,204
Next thing I knew,
Kristin was on the floor.

772
00:38:16,206 --> 00:38:18,861
It just...happened.

773
00:38:26,565 --> 00:38:30,917
And then I did what
I always do when I'm in trouble.

774
00:38:31,004 --> 00:38:32,745
I called daddy.

775
00:38:34,877 --> 00:38:37,445
He said he knew someone
who could fix it.

776
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:39,752
Ah, the fixer.

777
00:38:42,145 --> 00:38:44,104
You can let Cavalleri go now.

778
00:38:44,191 --> 00:38:45,497
[whispers]
Watch.

779
00:38:54,854 --> 00:38:57,335
Oh, my God.

780
00:39:00,425 --> 00:39:02,252
He's dead.

781
00:39:04,951 --> 00:39:06,344
Yeah.

782
00:39:14,177 --> 00:39:16,484
You abused a corpse
to get a confession.

783
00:39:16,571 --> 00:39:19,835
Used. Used a corpse.
There's no Ab.

784
00:39:19,922 --> 00:39:22,882
I'm appalled. I'm..

785
00:39:22,969 --> 00:39:24,797
I don't know what to say.

786
00:39:24,884 --> 00:39:26,581
Sir, it's not like
we killed him.

787
00:39:26,668 --> 00:39:28,496
His neck was broken
in the crash.

788
00:39:28,583 --> 00:39:31,673
- We got a confession.
- Suppose you didn't.

789
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:34,241
Suppose you'd been wrong.

790
00:39:34,328 --> 00:39:36,243
Have you any idea
of the vastness

791
00:39:36,330 --> 00:39:38,463
of the crapstorm
that would follow?

792
00:39:38,550 --> 00:39:40,290
It would blot out the sun.

793
00:39:40,378 --> 00:39:42,423
Sir, Crew and Batson
manipulated us

794
00:39:42,510 --> 00:39:44,251
into arresting
the wrong person.

795
00:39:44,338 --> 00:39:47,385
They bugged our offices
and subverted our case.

796
00:39:47,472 --> 00:39:49,474
I don't think we did
anything wrong.

797
00:39:49,561 --> 00:39:50,779
I think
we should be commended.

798
00:39:50,866 --> 00:39:53,434
[scoffs]

799
00:39:53,521 --> 00:39:55,784
Congratulations. You finally
got her to drink the Kool-Aid.

800
00:40:00,136 --> 00:40:01,660
Check yourself, agent.

801
00:40:03,836 --> 00:40:05,141
All of you.

802
00:40:09,015 --> 00:40:10,364
Well, I thought
that went pretty well.

803
00:40:10,451 --> 00:40:12,061
Great. Yeah.

804
00:40:12,148 --> 00:40:14,847
Highlight for me
was definitely your speech.

805
00:40:14,934 --> 00:40:18,894
Passionate. Articulate. Strong.

806
00:40:18,981 --> 00:40:20,243
Whatever.

807
00:40:21,331 --> 00:40:22,463
Hmm.

808
00:40:30,993 --> 00:40:33,822
Hey, good work with McAdoo,
you know, keeping him here.

809
00:40:33,909 --> 00:40:35,476
Yeah.

810
00:40:35,563 --> 00:40:38,348
You know...if boss
had given me a chance

811
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:39,741
I think I could have
gotten him to confess.

812
00:40:39,828 --> 00:40:42,396
Sure, if he wasn't,
you know, innocent.

813
00:40:42,483 --> 00:40:43,658
If it wasn't
for that small fact

814
00:40:43,745 --> 00:40:45,834
I'm sure you'd have
taken him to town.

815
00:40:45,921 --> 00:40:48,750
Thanks.

816
00:40:48,837 --> 00:40:50,709
You have any plans
for tonight?

817
00:40:50,796 --> 00:40:52,754
Home. TV.

818
00:40:52,841 --> 00:40:55,104
Well...have fun.

819
00:40:56,018 --> 00:40:57,455
You, too.

820
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:02,372
You're gonna die alone.

821
00:41:07,203 --> 00:41:08,553
- 'Uh, sir..'
- Morning.

822
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:09,815
Sir, you can't go in there.

823
00:41:09,902 --> 00:41:12,382
No, it's okay.
I come in peace.

824
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:15,647
- Great color on you.
- Y-you..

825
00:41:15,734 --> 00:41:18,780
- Go away.
- Just give me a minute, please.

826
00:41:18,867 --> 00:41:22,218
I-I want you, and I want your
team to know...that I got it.

827
00:41:22,305 --> 00:41:24,046
I got the message.

828
00:41:24,133 --> 00:41:25,483
I got it.

829
00:41:27,136 --> 00:41:31,489
The Red John case...belongs
to you.

830
00:41:31,576 --> 00:41:34,317
- You're gonna leave us alone?
- Yeah, that's right.

831
00:41:34,404 --> 00:41:37,625
- I don't believe that.
- I bought you doughnuts.

832
00:41:37,712 --> 00:41:39,975
'The international
law enforcement'

833
00:41:40,062 --> 00:41:41,803
symbol of friendship.

834
00:41:43,370 --> 00:41:46,504
I-I am trusting you
to catch Red John.

835
00:41:49,376 --> 00:41:52,292
I'm counting on it.

836
00:41:52,379 --> 00:41:54,990
We will catch him.
Thanks.

837
00:41:57,123 --> 00:41:58,516
Good hunting.

838
00:42:01,388 --> 00:42:03,956
Hicks, take that away.
Take it far away.

839
00:42:04,043 --> 00:42:06,567
Take it out of the building.
God knows what he put in there.

840
00:42:06,654 --> 00:42:08,177
You got it.

841
00:42:08,264 --> 00:42:10,615
Alright, let's go over
the most recent forensics.

842
00:42:10,702 --> 00:42:12,355
There are two short,
linear incised wounds

843
00:42:12,442 --> 00:42:14,140
that are extremely superficial.

844
00:42:14,227 --> 00:42:17,186
'They involve the anterior
surface of the right wrist'

845
00:42:17,273 --> 00:42:19,885
'which measures 0.8 inches.'

846
00:42:25,499 --> 00:42:27,240
[male #2]
'Okay, you got it.

847
00:42:27,327 --> 00:42:28,807
[Bosco]
'Don't tell the local guys
what it's for.'

848
00:42:28,894 --> 00:42:30,678
[male #2]
'Yeah, no worries.'

849
00:42:30,765 --> 00:42:32,550
[Bosco]
'Just say you're following up
on something.'

850
00:42:32,637 --> 00:42:34,769
'I want to keep this
on the down low for now.'

851
00:42:34,856 --> 00:42:38,077
'Now, what else did you get
from handwriting analysis?'

852
00:42:38,164 --> 00:42:40,906
[male #3]
'We've had two guys look at it.
One local, one from DC.'

853
00:42:40,993 --> 00:42:43,691
'And of course, they agree
on pretty much nothing.'

854
00:42:43,778 --> 00:42:47,129
[Bosco chuckles]
'Figures.
What did the DC Guysay?'

855
00:42:55,921 --> 00:42:56,617
[theme music]

